WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.167
-Jalyn Hall,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.100
-Thank you, thank you.
-I'm happy to meet you.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.100
I'm happy to get to know you.
I'm happy you're here.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.300
-Oh, not as much as I am.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.734
I will tell everybody right now,

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:13.000
I am so nervous to be in
all of your acquaintance.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.234
-Oh, my -- Don't be nervous.
You...

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.300
We're happy you're here.
Congratulations.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.367
You got nominated for two
NAACP Image Awards for "Till."

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:24.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.901
Two.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.400
The cast was also nominated.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.667
Last night, you were at the
Critics' Choice Awards,

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.934
so thank you for flying
all the way over back here.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.234
-Of course.
-Come on.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.367
You just turned 16, you said,

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.534
and you had a
red-carpet birthday party.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.000
-Yes.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.133
-Now, I've never heard of this
idea, but I think it's genius.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.534
-Thank you.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.834
-There it is, there, and there's
a giant poster of your name.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:47.300
-Yes.
-Now, who thought of this?

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.367
Whose idea was this?

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.067
-Well, initially,
I did have a vision.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.968
But I wish I could say that
I did it all myself,

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.167
but that was the work of

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.767
my beautiful and
super-talented mother.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.100
-Aww.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.300
You do have a
beautiful, super-talented --

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.767
-Thank you.
-I met your mom backstage.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:09.934
-Yes.
-Is mom here?

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.267
Is mom in the audience?
-Yes.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.601
-There's mom right there.
Hey, mom!

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:16.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:21.100
Look at him. Come on.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.200
We were talking backstage
of how proud she is of you.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.434
-Yes.
-And she should be.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:29.300
When you're not working,
I hear that you're a big gamer.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.334
I hear that you're a sports fan.
You make music.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.133
-Yes, yes, yes.
All of the above.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.868
-Yeah. Were you
thinking about going into

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.934
a different career
besides acting?

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.200
-Oh, man.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.133
I definitely have some, like,
thoughts about it,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.334
but, if anything,
I feel like acting is

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.767
a really good outlet to do a

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.734
bunch of the things
that you love.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:47.901
Like you said, sports.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:51.567
I'm actually starring in
the show "The Crossover"

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:55.834
coming to Disney on April 4th
and the next day on Disney+.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
And it's about basketball.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:01:59.667
And I get to play basketball.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.200
And I'm really excited
about that,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.834
because I got to fall in love
with the sport all over again.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.167
-I'm terrible at basketball.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.100
-R-- No!
-I tried so hard.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.234
I tried so hard. I really tried.
I just had nothing.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.601
I mean,
it was just embarrassing.

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:14.067
Terrible.
-I don't believe that.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.167
Come on.
Look how athletic he is.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:19.767
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.801
-Look at what
a great actor he is.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.501
Unbelievable.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:25.767
Oh, you know what
we've got to talk about?

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:27.367
This just got announced,
that you're going to play

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:28.834
young Martin Luther King Jr.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:31.100
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.367
-What a great day
to have you on.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:33.400
-Thank you, thank you.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.601
-You've got to be
excited about this.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:35.701
-Yes, very excited.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.901
-Martin Luther King
and Emmett Till.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.167
I mean,
these are very important people.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:44.300
-Yes. Going in this trajectory
has been an honor for me,

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.133
because there have been
a multitude of people

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.934
who have interpreted these roles
and did amazing jobs.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:55.200
So there's kind of that -- you
know, that standard to be set.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.200
But I welcome that challenge
with open arms,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.367
because I feel like you can
never get enough of interpreting

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.501
these people who helped
shape our world,

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:05.100
especially Emmett Till
and Martin Luther King.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.834
So I'm in love with
what I'm doing right now.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:11.467
-You're going to crush it, bud.
I saw "Till," and...

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:14.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
...everybody's amazing.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.734
-Thank you.
-Everybody's amazing in that.

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:18.434
We had Whoopi Goldberg
on the show,

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.901
and she's one of the producers.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.634
-I've always labeled myself as
a very, like, outgoing person.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:23.801
I love to make conversation.

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:25.901
But when it's Whoopi Goldberg,
you're like,

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:28.367
how do you start a conversation?

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.634
But long story short,
I really got to talk to her,

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.534
and she is super-hilarious.

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:36.601
She's herself 100% of the time.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.300
-But one day, when we were
filming, I was like,

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.167
"Can you really --
Can you meet my mother?"

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:42.634
Because I knew if I was nervous,

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.767
my mom was
beyond nervous, right?

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.067
So, I bring my mom over.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:49.200
And my mom's like, "Oh, my God,
that's Whoopi Goldberg."

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.934
She has this, like,
super-huge smile on her face.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:55.968
And she walks up to her
and she bows at Whoopi Goldberg.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.267
Right in the middle of set.

00:03:58.267 --> 00:03:59.868
They're setting up
the next shot.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:00.934
She's like...

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.834
I'm like, "Do your thing."
I mean...

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:05.501
-That's it.
Bow to Whoopi Goldberg.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.501
That's exactly right.
Come on, why not?

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:08.701
It's Whoopi.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.434
-She's an icon.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:11.868
-But she's
so humble and so nice.

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:13.133
-She's the best.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:17.968
-And Danielle Deadwyler,
who plays Emmett's mother --

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.434
she's going to be here
tomorrow night.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.167
Anything that I should --
that happened with her

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:22.701
that I should ask her about
on set or off set?

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.267
-Oh, man.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.067
Well, of course I know
you're going to ask her about

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:29.133
what a great actor she is,
but you should also ask her

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.400
about what
a great singer she is.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.033
She will not admit it, but she
has the voice of an angel,

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:37.434
and I really hope that you guys
encourage her to sing for you.

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.534
-Really? Alright.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.167
Alright, we'll try that.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:42.300
-We'll just do it.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.634
I won't even put it in
the questions.

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.601
I'm just gonna ask her to sing.

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:47.567
How do we get into this?

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.300
How do we set this up, "Till"?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:53.467
-It has been in the works
way longer than me.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:57.367
Mamie Till-Mobley
really wanted this movie

00:04:57.367 --> 00:05:01.133
to be made herself in 1955.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:06.067
And she had multiple deals,
but it always fell through.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:09.367
And I know for sure,
for over 30 years,

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.734
Keith Beauchamp has been
trying to do the same thing.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:14.334
And it's just now coming
into fruition.

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:18.234
And I am so, so thankful to be
a part of that conversation

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.868
and to be a part of
this movement and this message.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.167
And there's this scene
in the movie

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:26.868
where Mamie tells Emmett
to be small.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:30.534
And I think to myself,
the limitations put on

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:34.634
a 14-year-old boy to be small
is really heartbreaking,

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.467
you know, because what we want
to be in this day and age,

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.801
we want to be our full selves.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:41.167
We want to be amazing.
We want to be stars.

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:44.901
And it was -- It really stuck
with me, what she said.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:50.100
So I vow from now on,
as a black boy in America,

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.434
as anyone should, no matter your
race, is never be small.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.634
Shine your light
like this guy right here, huh?

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:57.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.167
-I'm not gonna be small, right?

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:00.901
-Never be small.
-No.

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:03.133
You're fantastic in this movie.
-Thank you.

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.701
-Everyone should go see
this movie.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.367
Everyone's performance is great.
Here's a clip.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:09.334
Here's Jalyn Hall in "Till."
Take a look at this.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:12.133
-When you get down there --
-Oh, not again, Mama.

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:13.667
I've already been to
Mississippi.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.067
-Only one time before,

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:18.100
and you started a fight with
another little boy.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.934
-He was p-picking on me.

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:22.834
-You're in the right to
stand up for yourself,

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:25.334
but that's not what
I'm talking about.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.033
Well...

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.634
they have a different set of
rules for Negroes down there.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:33.400
Are you listening?

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.701
-Yes.

00:06:35.701 --> 00:06:38.000
-You have to be extra careful
with white people.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.934
You can't risk looking at them
the wrong way.

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:41.868
-I know.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:46.334
-Bo...

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:48.934
be small down there.

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:52.334
-Like this?

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:54.801
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:56.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:56.267 --> 00:06:57.501
-Jalyn Hall.

00:06:57.501 --> 00:07:00.133
"Till" is on digital
and on demand

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:01.968
and available on
Blu-ray tomorrow.

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:05.033
We'll be right back with a
performance from Sudan Archives.

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:06.300
Stick around, everybody.

